    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0406" n="282" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg282"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7353b W 52/77: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-27T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 27,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>68. Lisbon Legation reports<anchor n="78" xml:id="d172-f1"/> that on March 21 the
                    British Minister to Portugal made a strong protest to the Prime Minister against
                        <pb facs="0407" n="283" xml:id="pg283"/> the granting of cable concessions
                    to the American companies. Try to secure an early answer to our last note to the
                    British Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
